### 🔸 **3. Palindrome (Handles String & Number)**

**Unified version that handles both strings and numbers**:

```js
function isPalindrome(input) {
  const str = input.toString();
  let left = 0, right = str.length - 1;
  while (left < right) {
    if (str[left++] !== str[right--]) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

